{"parentUuid":"33e611df-bb00-467d-ab3f-33e1120105cc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Py35VTTnhCXsitqTHpNKjX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N9ZoT1zWWG46tnCLr8kB91","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Google DeepMind Amazon ML scheduling combinatorial optimization production 2024 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7896,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":334,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7896},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7896,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoovt17nZhvSYK92nKPU","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c90524f-b755-4ebf-805f-1d1f916bf895","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:54.450Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"068ddc31-ecd9-4e6f-a05a-9ced0ab030bc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AB6g8Qb9ptPrf57gtiokrJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ML4CO survey 2025 machine learning combinatorial optimization review\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"[2203.02433] The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Competition (ML4CO): Results and Insights\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02433\"},{\"title\":\"ML4CO-Bench-101: Benchmark Machine Learning for ...\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/attachment?id=ye4ntB1Kzi&name=pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - GeminiLight/ml4co-survey: A survey on machine learning for combinatorial optimization. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/GeminiLight/ml4co-survey\"},{\"title\":\"The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization ...\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v176/gasse22a/gasse22a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Poster ML4CO-Bench-101: Benchmark Machine Learning for Classic Combinatorial Problems on Graphs\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/121381\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Competition (ML4CO): Results and Insights | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/The-Machine-Learning-for-Combinatorial-Optimization-Gasse-Cappart/c017ca4b90ac06e641269a9e8a29feaa655d4b9d\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Competition (ML4CO): Results and Insights\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/359054883_The_Machine_Learning_for_Combinatorial_Optimization_Competition_ML4CO_Results_and_Insights\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ds4dm/ml4co-competition: Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization - NeurIPS'21 competition\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ds4dm/ml4co-competition\"},{\"title\":\"The Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Competition (ML4CO): Results and Insights\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v176/gasse22a.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ML4CO (Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization):\n\n## Overview\n\nRecent years have seen a surge of interest in using machine learning as a new approach for solving combinatorial problems, either directly as solvers or by enhancing exact solvers. The ML4CO aims at improving state-of-the-art combinatorial optimization solvers by replacing key heuristic components, and the competition featured three challenging tasks: finding the best feasible solution, producing the tightest optimality certificate, and giving an appropriate solver configuration.\n\n## Current Research and Benchmarks\n\nThere are several active resources in the field:\n\n1. **ML4CO-Bench-101**: Combinatorial problems on graphs have attracted extensive efforts from the machine learning community over the past decade, and despite notable progress under the umbrella of ML4CO, a comprehensive categorization, unified reproducibility, and transparent evaluation protocols are still lacking for the emerging pool of neural CO solvers. ML4CO-Bench-101 collates a total of 65 datasets for 7 mainstream CO problems including both edge-oriented tasks (TSP, ATSP, CVRP) as well as node-oriented tasks (MIS, MCl, MVC, MCut).\n\n2. **Methodological Approaches**: Graph neural networks are highly effective for combinatorial optimization, while generative models like diffusion and consistency models generate results through progressive denoising processes.\n\n3. **Community Resources**: There are curated collections of ML4CO papers from top conferences, organized by method types, available on GitHub repositories dedicated to surveying the field.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"21b0036f-dd11-48f5-98ea-920b18968b54","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:59.963Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"068ddc31-ecd9-4e6f-a05a-9ced0ab030bc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cc7b842f-19ca-4451-8d10-738bfdff9c4a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PfoF56VNU1buwAEMyDkh6o","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NeuroSAT 2024 2025 industrial benchmark SAT competition GNN\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Published in Transactions on Machine Learning Research (05/2024)\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=7VB5db72lr\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-GATv2: A Dynamic Attention-Based Graph Neural Network for Solving Boolean Satisfiability Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/14/3/423\"},{\"title\":\"G4SATBench: Benchmarking and Advancing SAT Solving with Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2309.16941\"},{\"title\":\"1 Introduction\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.01173\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - zhaoyu-li/G4SATBench: [TMLR 2024] G4SATBench: Benchmarking and Advancing SAT Solving with Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/zhaoyu-li/G4SATBench\"},{\"title\":\"On the Expressive Power of GNNs for Boolean Satisfiability\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.08745\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Rank the Initial Branching Order of SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2603.07176v1\"},{\"title\":\"NEURAL NETWORKS AND THE SATISFIABILITY PROBLEM A DISSERTATION\",\"url\":\"https://users.cs.utah.edu/~tch/notes/PSSAT/IR/SAT/SAT-NN.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"HyperSAT: Unsupervised Hypergraph Neural Networks for Weighted MaxSAT Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.11885\"},{\"title\":\"000 001 002 003 004 005 006 007 008 009 010 011 012 013 014 015 016 017 018 019\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf/2506e22bfc230841780b46c4c63e8f68ce59b1c8.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about NeuroSAT, GNN-based SAT solving, and benchmarking efforts:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**G4SATBench Framework (2024)**\n\nG4SATBench is a framework that enables comprehensive comparisons and evaluations of various GNN-based SAT solvers. It currently consists of 7 datasets sourced from 3 distinct domain areas: random problems, pseudo-industrial problems, and combinatorial problems.\n\nThe framework utilizes the SR generator in NeuroSAT and the 3-SAT generator in CNFGen to produce random CNF formulas. For pseudo-industrial problems, they employ the Community Attachment (CA) model and the Popularity-Similarity (PS) model, which generate synthetic instances that exhibit similar statistical features to those observed in real-world industrial SAT instances.\n\n**NeuroSAT and Industrial Benchmarks**\n\nResearchers tested WL-powerful GNNs using random instances from the G4SAT benchmark as well as industrial and crafted instances from the International SAT competition. Competition instances often require more iterations, and sometimes WL-powerful GNNs are simply not expressive enough to predict a satisfying assignment.\n\n**Recent Developments (2024-2025)**\n\nSAT-GATv2 achieves an accuracy improvement of 1.75–5.51% over NeuroSAT on challenging random 3-SAT(n) instances. The research community continues to advance GNN-based approaches for SAT solving with various architectural improvements beyond the original NeuroSAT framework.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cba0d3a5-5bad-4c44-bfaa-85d0893f4261","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:01.183Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc7b842f-19ca-4451-8d10-738bfdff9c4a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3c90524f-b755-4ebf-805f-1d1f916bf895","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9ZoT1zWWG46tnCLr8kB91","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google DeepMind Amazon ML scheduling combinatorial optimization production 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A Gemini-powered coding agent for designing advanced algorithms — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/\"},{\"title\":\"Publications — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/research/publications/\"},{\"title\":\"Discovering Heuristics with Large Language Models (LLMs ...\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Heuristics_Discovery_Via_LLMs_CetinkayaBuyuktahtakinetal2025_OptOnline.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Research — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/research/\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: an open-source evolutionary framework for algorithmic discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v3\"},{\"title\":\"Gemini Deep Think: Redefining the Future of Scientific Research — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/accelerating-mathematical-and-scientific-discovery-with-gemini-deep-think/\"},{\"title\":\"Quantum-Guided Cluster Algorithms for Combinatorial Optimization | AWS Quantum Technologies Blog\",\"url\":\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/quantum-computing/quantum-guided-cluster-algorithms-for-combinatorial-optimization/\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_DeepMind\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind at ICML 2024 — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/google-deepmind-at-icml-2024/\"},{\"title\":\"AI as a research partner: Advancing theoretical computer science with AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/blog/ai-as-a-research-partner-advancing-theoretical-computer-science-with-alphaevolve/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding Google DeepMind, machine learning scheduling, and combinatorial optimization in 2024-2025:\n\n## Key Developments\n\n**AlphaEvolve for Combinatorial Optimization**\n\nGoogle DeepMind introduced AlphaEvolve, a closed-source system that generalizes from evolving single functions to entire codebases and a broader range of optimization tasks, including GPU kernels, warehouse-scale computing, and complexity theory. This AI agent evolves algorithms for math and practical applications in computing by combining the creativity of large language models with automated evaluators.\n\n**Production Applications**\n\nAlphaEvolve combines genetic algorithms with the Gemini family of LLMs to discover solutions across diverse domains, including data-center optimization, matrix multiplication, and combinatorial constructions. This indicates that the system has been applied to practical production challenges like data center optimization.\n\n**Research Breakthroughs in Combinatorial Optimization**\n\nAn advanced version of Gemini Deep Think helped resolve long-standing bottlenecks across algorithms, ML and combinatorial optimization, information theory, and economics through collaboration with experts on 18 research problems.\n\n**AWS Integration**\n\nThe search results also show that experiments were conducted using AWS Sagemaker with fixed computational budgets of vCPUS and RAM.\n\nThe results demonstrate that Google DeepMind has made significant advances in using AI agents for scheduling and combinatorial optimization problems, with practical applications in warehouse-scale computing and data center optimization during 2024-2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c6ac3913-5a26-458e-95a9-948bcaeb12f8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:01.812Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3c90524f-b755-4ebf-805f-1d1f916bf895","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"33e611df-bb00-467d-ab3f-33e1120105cc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmX772UUScLeAi7UvwZQys","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"learning to branch CP-SAT MIP 2024 2025 reinforcement learning\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning in MIP Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://co-at-work.zib.de/slides/COatWork2024_Berthold_MLinMIP.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Branch with Offline Reinforcement Learning | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=uHVIxJGwr4\"},{\"title\":\"[2411.19517v4] RL-MILP Solver: A Reinforcement Learning Approach for Solving Mixed-Integer Linear Programs with Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.19517v4\"},{\"title\":\"Reinforcement Learning for Ising Models: Datasets and Benchmark\",\"url\":\"https://ml4physicalsciences.github.io/2025/files/NeurIPS_ML4PS_2025_245.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"[2411.19517v2] RL-MILP Solver: A Reinforcement Learning Approach for Solving Mixed-Integer Linear Programs with Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.19517v2\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"}]\n\nI've found several relevant research results on learning to branch with reinforcement learning in MIP and constraint programming contexts. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent Research on Learning to Branch with Reinforcement Learning\n\n**Learning to Branch with Offline RL (2024)**\n\nA novel offline RL algorithm has been proposed for neural branching in branch-and-bound algorithm in mixed integer programming. Mixed Integer Linear Program (MILP) solvers are built upon a branch-and-bound (B&B) algorithm, where the efficiency of traditional solvers heavily depends on hand-craft heuristics for branching, which significantly limits success because such heuristics are often difficult to obtain and not easy to generalize across domains/problems.\n\n**RL-MILP Solver (2024-2025)**\n\nA novel reinforcement learning (RL)-based solver has been proposed that finds the first feasible solution and incrementally discovers better feasible solutions without delegating the remainder to off-the-shelf solvers. This approach addresses challenges with both binary and non-binary integer variables.\n\n## Related Work in Machine Learning for Optimization\n\nResearchers have introduced reinforcement learning approaches that strategically direct computational effort towards the most promising regions within the search space to enhance search efficiency.\n\n## CP-SAT Context\n\nCP-SAT employs Branch and Cut techniques, including linear relaxations and cutting planes, as part of its toolkit. This makes it relevant to branching strategies research in constraint programming.\n\nThe search results show active research in 2024-2025 applying reinforcement learning to improve branching decisions in MIP solvers, addressing the challenge of replacing hand-crafted heuristics with learned strategies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"899c9250-c3a0-4797-aae2-cdbb31e68335","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:04.314Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"33e611df-bb00-467d-ab3f-33e1120105cc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
