{"parentUuid":"9647510d-0698-4db3-8c78-975f3f8cc353","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013h2F7fmWEr9omuZfcaaA17","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N4hXobiv3tVtz2UBss6suq","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co","prompt":"List the most recent (2024-2025) papers categorized by task type: learning to branch, learning to cut, learning warm starts, end-to-end neural solvers, GNN for SAT/CSP, RL for branching. For each category, note maturity level (production-ready vs research-only) if mentioned."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6310,"cache_read_input_tokens":25587,"output_tokens":441,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6310},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":25587,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6310,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaooxxbkbhLRfG91Gj4iP","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4ddfbb5f-cbbf-45be-ae84-13d8312ff7bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:24.069Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"22267dec-c1e4-4af2-8b4f-5928133a4742","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q8KLzVStX8GFoGg7AoQCXK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"contrastive learning\" OR \"imitation learning\" branching variable selection MIP 2024 sample size\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2402.03647\"},{\"title\":\"CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=K6kt50zAiG&noteId=eAKTDVd6fy\"},{\"title\":\"[2402.03647v1] CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03647v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2402.03647] CAMBranch: Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03647\"},{\"title\":\"TOWARDS IMITATION LEARNING TO BRANCH FOR MIP\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/file/850cc7c4e5619fdc2f30c4eaa5ce3c17-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Imitation Learning to Branch for MIP: A Hybrid Reinforcement Learning based Sample Augmentation Approach | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=NdcQQ82mfy\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2024 L2P-MIP: LEARNING TO PRESOLVE FOR\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=McfYbKnpT8\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR Poster Towards Imitation Learning to Branch for MIP: A Hybrid Reinforcement Learning based Sample Augmentation Approach\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/virtual/2024/poster/18781\"},{\"title\":\"Intelligent Variable Selection for Branch & Bound Methods\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=U3cYyMKZxVP\"},{\"title\":\"Learning efficient branch-and-bound for solving Mixed Integer Linear Programs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1568494625001747\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found several highly relevant papers from 2024 that combine contrastive learning and imitation learning for branching variable selection in Mixed Integer Programming (MIP):\n\n## Key Finding: CAMBranch\n\nCAMBranch proposes Contrastive Learning with Augmented MILPs for Branching, a framework that generates Augmented MILPs (AMILPs) by applying variable shifting to limited expert data from their original MILPs. CAMBranch leverages both MILPs and AMILPs for imitation learning and employs contrastive learning to enhance the model's ability to capture MILP features, thereby improving the quality of branching decisions.\n\n## Sample Size Impact\n\nA key advantage of this approach is its efficiency regarding sample size. CAMBranch, trained with only 10% of the complete dataset, exhibits superior performance. This is significant because collecting expert samples for imitation learning, particularly for Strong Branching, is a time-consuming endeavor.\n\n## Related Approaches (2024)\n\nAnother complementary 2024 work addresses similar challenges through a novel hybrid online and offline reinforcement learning (RL) approach to enhance the branching policy by cost-effective training sample augmentation.\n\nThese papers represent the current state-of-the-art in combining contrastive and imitation learning approaches for MIP branching decisions, with a focus on reducing sample collection costs through data augmentation strategies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ce0d6774-29ef-4671-9f64-f2db2f8871c5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:28.320Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"22267dec-c1e4-4af2-8b4f-5928133a4742","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"30e2c4b5-1de4-4dd1-bce1-8d1c8c32fee2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VQK87h9n9zqYyMfZ3mbCcu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LLM heuristic discovery FunSearch AlphaEvolve combinatorial optimization 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Magellan: Autonomous Discovery of Novel Compiler Optimization Heuristics with AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2601.21096v1\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: an open-source evolutionary framework for algorithmic discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v4\"},{\"title\":\"Can We Use AI to Discover Better Algorithms? | Richard Cornelius Suwandi\",\"url\":\"https://richardcsuwandi.github.io/blog/2025/llm-algorithm-discovery/\"},{\"title\":\"2025-5-16 AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://msu.dvaoblaka.ru/media/2025/05/68271bf34ef55_AlphaEvolve.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/AlphaEvolve.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"HeurAgenix: Leveraging LLMs for Solving Complex Combinatorial Optimization Challenges\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.15196v1\"},{\"title\":\"EvoLattice: Persistent Internal-Population Evolution through Multi-Alternative Quality-Diversity Graph Representations for LLM-Guided Program Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2512.13857\"},{\"title\":\"This is the author’s version of the work accepted in Nature.\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/Mathematical-discoveries-from-program-search-with-large-language-models.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"HeuriGym: An Agentic Benchmark for LLM-Crafted Heuristics ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cornell.edu/gomes/pdf/2025_chen_arxiv_heurigym.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Global Optimization for Combinatorial Geometry Problems ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.05943\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about LLM heuristic discovery, FunSearch, AlphaEvolve, and combinatorial optimization in 2025:\n\n## FunSearch Foundation\n\nFunSearch demonstrated that combining an LLM with evolutionary program search can discover improved solutions to traditional combinatorial optimization problems such as cap set and bin packing through iterative program refinement. FunSearch demonstrated the existence of hitherto unknown constructions that go beyond existing ones, including the largest improvement in 20 years to the asymptotic lower bound, showing the first scientific discovery using an LLM.\n\n## AlphaEvolve Advancement\n\nAlphaEvolve, powered by Novikov et al. (2025), evolves compiler passes by synthesizing and evaluating executable C++ heuristics with a simple integration pass into existing compilers. Unlike FunSearch, which focuses on discovering single functions, AlphaEvolve is designed to evolve entire codebases and develop much more intricate algorithms.\n\nAlphaEvolve uses an ensemble approach combining Gemini Flash and Gemini Pro, where the lightweight Gemini Flash enables higher rates of candidate generation through lower latency, while the more powerful Gemini Pro provides deeper insights and higher-quality suggestions.\n\n## Mathematical and Optimization Results\n\nIn 75% of cases AlphaEvolve rediscovered the best known constructions, and in 20% of cases it discovered a new object that is better than a previously known best construction, thereby improving the SOTA.\n\n## Related Work in 2025\n\nGoogle DeepMind released AlphaEvolve capable of evolving entire codebases and producing SOTA solutions to a diverse range of problems, yet its closed-source nature and reliance on proprietary models hinders reproducibility. In response, several open-source projects have emerged to democratize these capabilities, such as OpenEvolve, ShinkaEvolve and ThetaEvolve.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"50c1e366-cfc1-4ad9-bf3e-41828bf3d185","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:29.102Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30e2c4b5-1de4-4dd1-bce1-8d1c8c32fee2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9647510d-0698-4db3-8c78-975f3f8cc353","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kt9bJ6SEhKkJJL6K4AeRCj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"XGBoost LightGBM solver configuration tuning algorithm portfolio 2024 SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"xgboost-lightgbm-hyperparameter-tuning/README.md at master · jia-zhuang/xgboost-lightgbm-hyperparameter-tuning\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jia-zhuang/xgboost-lightgbm-hyperparameter-tuning/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Light GBM model vs XGBoost Model Parameter Tuning and Examples\",\"url\":\"https://pyligent.github.io/2019-08-20-lightGBM_XGBoost/\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters Tuning — LightGBM 4.6.0.99 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://lightgbm.readthedocs.io/en/latest/Parameters-Tuning.html\"},{\"title\":\"Getting started with Gradient Boosting Machines - using XGBoost and LightGBM parameters\",\"url\":\"https://nityesh.com/gradient-boosting-machines-intro/\"},{\"title\":\"XGBoost Parameters Tuning\",\"url\":\"https://www.analyticsvidhya.com/blog/2016/03/complete-guide-parameter-tuning-xgboost-with-codes-python/\"},{\"title\":\"Which algorithm takes the crown: Light GBM vs XGBOOST?\",\"url\":\"https://www.analyticsvidhya.com/blog/2017/06/which-algorithm-takes-the-crown-light-gbm-vs-xgboost/\"},{\"title\":\"Auto XGBoost, Auto LightGBM, Auto CatBoost, Auto GradientBoosting\",\"url\":\"https://thierrymoudiki.github.io/blog/2024/08/05/python/r/unibooster\"},{\"title\":\"XGBoost: Theory and Hyperparameter Tuning | Towards Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://towardsdatascience.com/xgboost-theory-and-hyperparameter-tuning-bc4068aba95e/\"},{\"title\":\"SDS 771: Gradient Boosting: XGBoost, LightGBM and CatBoost, with Kirill Eremenko - SuperDataScience | Machine Learning | AI | Data Science Career | Analytics | Success\",\"url\":\"https://www.superdatascience.com/podcast/sds-771-gradient-boosting-xgboost-lightgbm-and-catboost-with-kirill-eremenko\"},{\"title\":\"XGBoost vs LightGBM: How Are They Different\",\"url\":\"https://neptune.ai/blog/xgboost-vs-lightgbm/\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for the query: \"XGBoost LightGBM solver configuration tuning algorithm portfolio 2024 SAT\"\n\nThe search results provide information about XGBoost and LightGBM parameter tuning and configuration, but the results focus primarily on hyperparameter tuning techniques for these gradient boosting algorithms rather than on the specific combination of topics in your query (particularly the \"algorithm portfolio\" and \"SAT\" aspects in a 2024 context).\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**XGBoost and LightGBM Parameter Tuning:**\n\nKey parameters for tuning include max_depth for both algorithms, and min_split_gain (LightGBM) or gamma (XGBoost) for minimum loss reduction required for tree splits. For LightGBM specifically, min_child_samples is a very important parameter to prevent overfitting.\n\n**Algorithm Differences:**\n\nLightGBM uses leaf-wise tree growth while many other tools use depth-wise growth, and the leaf-wise algorithm can converge much faster. LightGBM is generally faster and more memory-efficient for large datasets, while XGBoost may perform better with smaller datasets or when interpretability is crucial.\n\n**2024 Development:**\n\nAs of August 2024, unifiedbooster was created to provide a unified interface to XGBoost, CatBoost, LightGBM without worrying about different parameter names.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about \"solver configuration\" or \"algorithm portfolio\" in relation to SAT (Boolean satisfiability) in 2024. If you're looking for information about using these algorithms in SAT solving or algorithm selection contexts, you may need a more specific search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0ef0819f-5023-478d-a667-353b81a27f98","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:29.193Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9647510d-0698-4db3-8c78-975f3f8cc353","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4ddfbb5f-cbbf-45be-ae84-13d8312ff7bd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N4hXobiv3tVtz2UBss6suq","type":"tool_result","content":"# Recent Machine Learning for Combinatorial Optimization Papers (2024-2025)\n\nBased on the GitHub repository, here are the most recent papers organized by category:\n\n## Learning to Branch\nNo papers explicitly categorized under this specific heading appear in the 2024-2025 section, though branching-related work may fall under Mixed Integer Programming research.\n\n## Learning to Cut\nNot explicitly listed as a separate category in the recent papers shown.\n\n## Learning Warm Starts\n**\"A Neural Column Generation Approach to the Vehicle Routing Problem with Two-Dimensional\"** (IJCAI 2024) - addresses initialization strategies for routing problems.\n\n## End-to-End Neural Solvers\n\n- **\"Large Language Models as End-to-end Combinatorial Optimization Solvers\"** (NeurIPS 2025) - demonstrates LLM-based solution generation\n- **\"GLOP: Learning Global Partition and Local Construction\"** (AAAI 2024) - hierarchical approach for routing\n- **\"UDC: A Unified Neural Divide-and-Conquer Framework\"** (NeurIPS 2024) - demonstrates scalability techniques\n\n**Maturity Assessment:** Primarily research-stage; production applications remain limited due to scalability and reliability concerns.\n\n## GNN for SAT/CSP\nThe repository shows extensive GNN work but specific SAT/CSP papers from 2024-2025 aren't prominently featured in recent additions.\n\n## RL for Branching\n**\"Multi-Action Self-Improvement for Neural Combinatorial Optimization\"** (ICLR 2026) - employs reinforcement learning for solution refinement strategies across problem types.\n\n**Overall Maturity Level:** Research-dominant with emerging practical applications in vehicle routing and scheduling domains."}]},"uuid":"2c2f18d1-03dc-48ea-a801-7ef6fb2c3fc0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:31.035Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4ddfbb5f-cbbf-45be-ae84-13d8312ff7bd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2c2f18d1-03dc-48ea-a801-7ef6fb2c3fc0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af05282ff225ef9db","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DUa92ZSVcqiLycvAm3nU78","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material now. Let me synthesize the response.\n\n---\n\n# ML4CO 2024-2026 调研报告（聚焦 SAT/CSP）\n\n## 一、三大类划分\n\n### A. 成熟可用（可直接落地）\n\n| 方向 | 适用性打分 | 说明 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **GBDT 做候选排序 / 配置选择**（XGBoost、LightGBM） | **5/5** | 算法选择（algorithm selection）和 portfolio 路线已经成熟 10+ 年了，SATzilla 谱系一直在用。小样本（几百到几千）就能跑，工业 SAT solver 的参数自适应都是这个套路。完美匹配你们\"每天 10-30 个候选\"的样本量级。 |\n| **GNN 提取特征 + 浅层模型预测变量偏置/分支顺序**（MIP-GNN、Gasse 2019 谱系） | **4/5** | 双向二部图（变量-约束）→ GCN 提特征，是公认的\"OR 友好\"baseline。Ecole 库（基于 SCIP）有现成 pipeline。但要注意：CP-SAT 不是 SCIP，没暴露分支回调，你们能做的更多是 **候选排序 / warm start 顺序**，而不是 in-solver branching。 |\n| **Imitation learning + 数据增广**（CAMBranch, ICLR 2024） | **4/5** | 关键发现：CAMBranch 用 **10% 数据**就能超越完整数据训练。这对你们极其友好——证明了\"小样本 + 数据增广\"在 MIP 分支学习里行得通。 |\n\n### B. 实验室级（学术 SOTA，工业落地有限）\n\n| 方向 | 适用性打分 | 说明 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **GNN-based SAT solver（NeuroSAT 谱系）** | **2/5** | G4SATBench (TMLR 2024) 给出了诚实结论：在 random / pseudo-industrial 上能跑，在 SAT competition **真实 industrial 实例**上 WL-powerful GNN 表达力不够，还远不能替代 CDCL。SAT-GATv2 比 NeuroSAT 提升 1.75-5.51%，但起点本来就低。**不要把 NeuroSAT 当 solver 用，最多当 oracle 提示**。 |\n| **End-to-end 神经 CO solver（TSP/CVRP 路线）** | **1/5** | ICLR 2025 综述明确：训练在 100 节点，迁移到 200 节点就显著退化。和你们 70x70 + Benders 分解架构完全不匹配。**直接排除**。 |\n| **Offline RL learning to branch**（RL-MILP Solver, 2024） | **2/5** | 还在 MIPLIB 这种学术 benchmark 上较劲，工业落地证据弱。CP-SAT 不开放分支接口，没法直接接入。 |\n| **Pretrained GNN + finetune** | **2/5** | Stanford SNAP 的 gnn-pretrain 主要在分子/社交网络。CO 领域**没有事实标准的 pretrained model zoo**，HuggingFace 上没有像 BERT 那样可下载的\"通用 CO 模型\"。每个 CO 任务的图结构差异大，迁移效果差。 |\n\n### C. 还在研究（前沿，观望）\n\n| 方向 | 适用性打分 | 说明 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **LLM 演化算法发现**（FunSearch 2024, AlphaEvolve 2025） | **3/5** | DeepMind AlphaEvolve 在 bin packing、矩阵乘法、数据中心调度上有真实战果。开源版有 OpenEvolve / ShinkaEvolve / ThetaEvolve。**对你们\"启发式发现 / candidate ordering 函数\"是潜在大杀器**，但需要 LLM API 预算。 |\n| **Diffusion / Consistency model 做 CO** | **1/5** | ML4CO-Bench-101 (NeurIPS 2025) 提到，但全在图论 toy 任务（TSP/MIS/MVC）。 |\n| **Memory-Enhanced Neural Solvers**（MEMENTO, InstaDeep 2025） | **1/5** | routing-only。 |\n\n## 二、对你们计划书的关键修正建议\n\n你们计划书\"先不上深度学习，用 LightGBM/RF/XGBoost\"的判断 **基本正确**，但有 3 处可以加强：\n\n1. **\"GNN\" 要细分**：不要把 GNN 当成\"深度学习黑盒\"一起排除。**GNN 当特征提取器 + 浅层 head** 是工业 OR 的事实标准（MIP-GNN 路线），训练成本不高，和你们路线兼容。真正要避开的是 NeuroSAT 那种 end-to-end GNN solver。\n\n2. **CAMBranch 的小样本结论值得抄作业**：10% 数据 + contrastive augmentation 就能 work。你们每天 10-30 样本，攒一两周后用类似数据增广（变量平移、对称等价 MILP）能把有效样本量翻倍三倍。\n\n3. **LLM 演化是漏掉的方向**：你们 AI Safety Contract 列的几条（candidate ordering、UNKNOWN 分类、tuning 解释）刚好就是 AlphaEvolve / FunSearch 擅长的——**让 LLM 演化出 candidate ordering 的启发式函数本身**，比训一个 GNN 排序器风险更低（产出是可读 Python 代码，可审计），符合你们 shadow-only 安全约束。\n\n## 三、推荐深入的 3 个方向（按优先级）\n\n1. **GBDT-based candidate ordering + 数据增广**（最稳）：直接用 LightGBM 学 `(candidate特征) -> 求解时长/可行性` 的回归/分类，用 CAMBranch 风格做样本增广。1-2 周原型，0 风险。\n\n2. **MIP-GNN 风格的变量偏置预测做 warm-start hint**（中风险高回报）：CP-SAT 支持 `AddHint`，把 GNN 预测的变量偏置作为 hint 喂进去，**完全符合**你们 Safety Contract \"as hints, not constraints\"。Ecole 不直接支持 CP-SAT，但二部图特征可以自己抽。\n\n3. **LLM 演化 candidate ordering 函数（FunSearch/AlphaEvolve 风格）**（高潜力）：让 LLM 反复生成 Python 排序函数，用你们的真实 campaign 做 evaluator，挑分数最高的留下。产出物是可读代码，自然满足\"可审计、shadow-only、不写 checkpoint\"的合规要求。\n\n## 关键资源\n\n- [Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co](https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co) — 持续更新的 ML4CO 论文集\n- [G4SATBench (TMLR 2024)](https://arxiv.org/html/2309.16941) — GNN for SAT 的诚实 benchmark\n- [CAMBranch (ICLR 2024)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03647) — 小样本 + 数据增广做分支学习\n- [ML4CO-Bench-101 (NeurIPS 2025)](https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/121381) — 7 类 CO 问题统一 benchmark\n- [Ecole library](https://www.ecole.ai/) — Gasse 团队的 RL-for-MIP 接口（SCIP-based）\n- [Berthold 2024 - ML in MIP slides](https://co-at-work.zib.de/slides/COatWork2024_Berthold_MLinMIP.pdf) — FICO Xpress 视角的工业现状\n- [AlphaEvolve (DeepMind 2025)](https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/) — LLM 演化算法\n- [MIP-GNN 论文](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360961611_MIP-GNN_A_Data-Driven_Framework_for_Guiding_Combinatorial_Solvers) — 二部图 GNN warm-start 标准做法\n- [RL-MILP Solver (2024)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.19517v4) — RL 做 MIP 求解最新尝试"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5513,"cache_read_input_tokens":31897,"output_tokens":2958,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5513},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2958,"cache_read_input_tokens":31897,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5513,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caooz2BLAD38iZTDSDYW9","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d14c15e1-1f7d-47f3-bcc1-60a414d05c91","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:07:28.422Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
